WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:03.435
-After Special Counsel
Robert Mueller

00:00:03.435 --> 00:00:05.271
delivered his report,
President Trump decided

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:07.740
to pick fights over healthcare
and the Special Olympics.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.009
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:14.213
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.213 --> 00:00:16.849
It's been a little over a week
since Trump's Attorney General

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:19.352
William Barr released his letter
on Mueller's report,

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:22.155
stating that the investigation
did not establish that members

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:24.691
of the Trump campaign
conspired or coordinated

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:25.825
with the Russian government

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:27.660
in its election-interference
activities.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.829
And, obviously,
that was good news for Trump.

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:31.931
I'd say he's had
a pep in his step ever since,

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:33.833
but he doesn't really
take steps.

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:35.101
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.337
If he had a Fitbit,
the only thing his Fitbit

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:39.472
would ever display is, "You up?"

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:41.140
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:45.011
Now, when Barr released
this memo, everyone just assumed

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:47.013
it was a summary
of Mueller's full report,

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:49.182
a word Trump's aides
and the media

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:51.016
have used over and over again.

00:00:51.016 --> 00:00:54.253
-The Attorney General's summary
of the Mueller report is out.

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:56.889
-We received a 4-page summary
of the Mueller report.

00:00:56.889 --> 00:00:59.125
-This was a summary
of the Robert Mueller report.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:00.160
-Preview.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:03.096
-You have the Barr summary.

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:06.098
-The 4-page summary
by Attorney General Barr.

00:01:06.098 --> 00:01:08.568
-There you go -- this was
a summary of Mueller's report.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.570
Barr told us everything
we need to know,

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.505
and we can all move on.
Got it.

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:14.607
-The Attorney General tonight
sent this letter

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:17.009
announcing
that everybody misinterpreted

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:19.045
what he said last weekend
in that letter.

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:21.080
What he did last week
is being talked about

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.515
in a way that he didn't expect.

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:25.518
That's not at all what he meant,
and we should all know better.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:27.687
"I am aware
of some media reports

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:30.490
and other public statements
mischaracterizing

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:33.159
my March 24th
supplemental notification

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.561
as a summary of
the special counsel's

00:01:35.561 --> 00:01:36.896
investigation and report.

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:41.200
My March 24th letter was not
and did not purport to be

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.835
an exhaustive recounting

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:45.705
of the special counsel's
investigation or report.

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:48.474
-Wait. So it wasn't
supposed to be a summary?

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:50.643
That's kind of an important
detail to leave out.

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.745
That's like reading the line,
"The Prince and Princess

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.546
lived happily ever after,"
in a fairy tale,

00:01:54.546 --> 00:01:56.382
and then you turn the page
and there's a note saying,

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:57.917
"That was not and should not

00:01:57.917 --> 00:01:59.719
be mischaracterized
as the ending.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:02.355
They got divorced the next day."

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:06.358
Now, there is no --
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:02:06.358 --> 00:02:09.561
To be clear, there's no reason
to expect that Barr's memo

00:02:09.561 --> 00:02:11.463
is distorting Mueller's report.

00:02:11.463 --> 00:02:13.532
But even if his initial memo
was accurate

00:02:13.532 --> 00:02:16.001
and made in good faith,
it's still difficult for anyone

00:02:16.001 --> 00:02:18.104
to summarize something
as long as Mueller's report.

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:20.005
For one thing,
the report is apparently

00:02:20.005 --> 00:02:22.575
more than 300 pages long,
went well beyond the kind of

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:25.178
bare-bones summary required
by the Justice Department,

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:27.112
and detailed
his conclusions at length.

00:02:27.112 --> 00:02:30.516
And you can't boil a 300-page
document down to 4 pages.

00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:32.418
It's like when you try
to cram for a test

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:34.754
by reading the Cliff Notes
for "The Great Gatsby"

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:36.689
and you end up writing,
"Wealthy man enjoys

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:38.390
consequence-free summer
in the Hamptons."

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:39.759
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:42.929
So, we have no idea --
no idea -- what's in the report.

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:45.298
Barr says it'll be released
sometime this month,

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:47.633
and yet some Republicans
are already threatening to block

00:02:47.633 --> 00:02:50.770
the release of a report they say
exonerates the President.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:53.439
Last week, Senate Majority
Leader Mitch McConnell objected

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:56.309
to a resolution calling for
the report to be made public,

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:58.310
and Senator Rand Paul said
he would oppose

00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:00.513
releasing the report
until there's an investigation

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:02.415
of the Obama administration.

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:07.219
-We need to have information
on Obama White House officials,

00:03:07.219 --> 00:03:10.556
Comey, Brennan, Clapper.
That should be part of it.

00:03:10.556 --> 00:03:12.825
So, Democrats want
the complete Mueller report.

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:15.528
I'm going to object
until we get a complete report

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:18.865
of all the Obama-era officials
that got this thing started.

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:21.967
-You want an investigation
of the Obama administration?

00:03:21.967 --> 00:03:25.605
You investigated him for eight
years and came up with nothing.

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:27.273
The worst scandal you dug up

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:30.142
was the fact
that he wore a tan suit once.

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:32.512
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:32.512 --> 00:03:34.113
"Where did he get the suit?

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:36.549
How much did he pay
for the suit?"

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:38.250
So, Mueller's report
did not establish

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:40.186
that the Trump campaign
conspired with Russia.

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:41.954
But still, even if you put aside

00:03:41.954 --> 00:03:43.455
the question
of Russian collusion,

00:03:43.455 --> 00:03:46.826
Mueller's investigation
has still exposed a whole world

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:49.762
of normalized corruption
by some of the wealthiest

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:51.531
and most powerful people
in the country

00:03:51.531 --> 00:03:54.434
that was just accepted
in Washington until now.

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:56.602
Just look at Paul Manafort.
The guy spent years

00:03:56.602 --> 00:03:58.103
as an unregistered
foreign agent,

00:03:58.103 --> 00:03:59.939
lobbying for some of
the worst people in the world.

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:02.508
And in the process, he stole
tens of millions of dollars

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:04.644
from the American people,
money he used to buy everything

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:07.113
from antique rugs
to expensive cars to --

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:10.917
and this is real -- a $15,000
jacket made from an ostrich,

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:13.286
which is why
Manafort's heart dropped

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:16.188
when he walked into
the courtroom and saw the judge.

00:04:16.188 --> 00:04:19.191
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:19.191 --> 00:04:22.795
It shouldn't...

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:24.263
It shouldn't take
a special counsel

00:04:24.263 --> 00:04:26.599
for us to find out that some of
the most powerful people

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:28.200
in the country
are hoarding their wealth

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.636
by committing serial fraud

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:32.572
and illegally stashing their
money in offshore tax havens.

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:35.107
Even if nothing else came out
of the Russia investigation,

00:04:35.107 --> 00:04:37.577
people are learning how wealth
and power operate in America.

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:39.312
I mean, this guy right here

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:41.047
was the President's
campaign chairman.

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:42.482
The only way it could be worse

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:45.451
is if Trump made Lori Loughlin
his Secretary of Education.

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:46.752
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.752 --> 00:04:50.790
And I, of course --
I, of course am just kidding.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.658
Betsy DeVos is still worse.

00:04:52.658 --> 00:04:54.059
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.059 --> 00:04:59.231
I mean, at least...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:59.231 --> 00:05:01.967
At least Lori Loughlin's
trying to make it easier

00:05:01.967 --> 00:05:03.636
for people to get into college.

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:04.871
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.871 --> 00:05:06.772
In fact, even as Trump
and his inner circle

00:05:06.772 --> 00:05:08.874
has spent their time in power
enriching themselves,

00:05:08.874 --> 00:05:10.576
they've also been trying
to take healthcare away

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:11.643
from millions of people.

00:05:11.643 --> 00:05:12.945
Last week,
the Trump administration

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:14.647
said the entire
Affordable Care Act

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:16.983
should be repealed, and yet,
as if that wasn't enough,

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:19.652
the Trump administration
also decided

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:21.153
to pick
a totally unnecessary fight

00:05:21.153 --> 00:05:22.988
with basically everybody

00:05:22.988 --> 00:05:26.525
by proposing to cut funding
for the Special Olympics.

00:05:26.525 --> 00:05:29.027
-Education Secretary Betsy DeVos
came under fire

00:05:29.027 --> 00:05:31.030
on Capitol Hill Tuesday
while defending

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:33.833
proposed funding cuts
for the Special Olympic.

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:37.870
The Trump administration
wants to cut all $18 million

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.772
in federal money
for the program.

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:41.507
-How awful do you have to be

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:43.943
to try to cut funding
for the Special Olympics?

00:05:43.943 --> 00:05:46.211
You might as well
use the money you saved

00:05:46.211 --> 00:05:48.614
to bulldoze an orphanage.

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:50.582
"We all know
those orphanages are eyesores.

00:05:50.582 --> 00:05:51.784
We're knocking down them."

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:53.419
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:55.488
And the administration's
response to the news

00:05:55.488 --> 00:05:57.990
was also proof that
the President has no idea

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:59.125
what his own government
is doing.

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:01.326
First,
Education Secretary Betsy DeVos

00:06:01.326 --> 00:06:03.829
said it wasn't her idea
to make the cut

00:06:03.829 --> 00:06:06.732
and blasted Democrats
for making a political issue

00:06:06.732 --> 00:06:08.434
out of it
during a budget hearing.

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:11.103
-As I said then
and I'll say again,

00:06:11.103 --> 00:06:13.739
this week,
had to make tough choices

00:06:13.739 --> 00:06:16.375
and decisions
around the budget priorities.

00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:18.744
I love Special Olympics myself.

00:06:18.744 --> 00:06:22.314
I have given a portion of my
salary to Special Olympics.

00:06:22.314 --> 00:06:25.284
I hope all of this debate
encourages lots of

00:06:25.284 --> 00:06:28.020
private contributions
to Special Olympics.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:32.592
So let's not use
disabled children

00:06:32.592 --> 00:06:37.997
in a twisted way
for your political narrative.

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:41.467
That is just disgusting,
and it's shameful.

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:45.004
-You guys are the ones
who proposed the cut!

00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:46.839
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:06:46.839 --> 00:06:49.608
If you set --

00:06:49.608 --> 00:06:51.510
If you set
your neighbor's house on fire,

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:53.979
and they call 911,
you can't turn around and say,

00:06:53.979 --> 00:06:55.681
"Aren't you the town gossip!"

00:06:55.681 --> 00:06:57.616
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.616 --> 00:06:59.285
Also, can we go back to this?

00:06:59.285 --> 00:07:02.888
-I have given a portion of my
salary to Special Olympics.

00:07:02.888 --> 00:07:04.623
-You're a billionaire.

00:07:04.623 --> 00:07:07.159
The Special Olympics cut
was $18 million.

00:07:07.159 --> 00:07:09.128
Betsy DeVos has,
according to "Newsweek,"

00:07:09.128 --> 00:07:12.998
10 boats, 2 helicopters,
and a yacht scheduler.

00:07:12.998 --> 00:07:16.235
She has so many yachts,
she has a yacht scheduler.

00:07:16.235 --> 00:07:17.569
[ Laughter ]

00:07:17.569 --> 00:07:19.738
What's a yacht scheduler?!

00:07:19.738 --> 00:07:20.806
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:20.806 --> 00:07:23.709
Is it someone who --

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:27.946
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:27.946 --> 00:07:30.716
Is a yacht scheduler
someone who, when you say,

00:07:30.716 --> 00:07:32.819
"Bring the yacht around,"
says, "I wouldn't do that.

00:07:32.819 --> 00:07:34.387
It might crash
into the other yacht"?

00:07:34.387 --> 00:07:36.021
[ Laughter ]

00:07:36.021 --> 00:07:38.157
Then, after the hearing,
reporters tried to get answers

00:07:38.157 --> 00:07:40.092
from DeVos as she waited
for an elevator,

00:07:40.092 --> 00:07:42.361
and she responded by pretending
not to hear them.

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:44.230
-Madam Secretary,
do you any response

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.933
to the Democrats' criticism
of your budget proposal?

00:07:53.772 --> 00:07:56.542
Madam Secretary, you said today
that you were not the person

00:07:56.542 --> 00:07:59.445
that proposed
this funding change.

00:07:59.445 --> 00:08:02.782
Can you explain who
in your administration did?

00:08:05.584 --> 00:08:06.986
Madam Secretary,
have you spoken to the President

00:08:06.986 --> 00:08:09.021
about this at all?

00:08:14.226 --> 00:08:15.995
If there's some
misunderstanding,

00:08:15.995 --> 00:08:18.531
Madam Secretary, this is your
opportunity to explain it to us.

00:08:22.234 --> 00:08:24.803
-I mean, look at her.
That's the face

00:08:24.803 --> 00:08:28.107
of someone thinking to herself,
"Where's my elevator scheduler?"

00:08:28.107 --> 00:08:36.548
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:08:36.548 --> 00:08:39.518
-Also, I love how the camera
zooms in on her face.

00:08:39.518 --> 00:08:42.788
CNN apparently got the same
director who did "The Office."

00:08:42.788 --> 00:08:44.557
[ Laughter ]

00:08:44.557 --> 00:08:46.492
-Then after
his Education Secretary

00:08:46.492 --> 00:08:48.693
went to Capitol Hill
to defend a budget cut

00:08:48.693 --> 00:08:50.963
that basically everyone hated,
Trump just waltzed up

00:08:50.963 --> 00:08:52.298
to reporters
on the White House lawn

00:08:52.298 --> 00:08:53.466
and told them, "Never mind.

00:08:53.466 --> 00:08:55.434
We're funding
the Special Olympics after all."

00:08:55.434 --> 00:08:57.503
-Why cut money to the
Special Olympics?

00:08:57.503 --> 00:08:59.038
Why would you cut funding
for that?

00:08:59.038 --> 00:09:02.408
-The Special Olympics
will be funded.

00:09:02.408 --> 00:09:06.178
I just told my people I want
to fund the Special Olympics.

00:09:06.178 --> 00:09:10.449
And I just authorized a funding
of the Special Olympics.

00:09:10.449 --> 00:09:12.384
I've been
to the Special Olympics.

00:09:12.384 --> 00:09:13.853
I think it's incredible.

00:09:13.853 --> 00:09:15.988
And I just authorized a funding.

00:09:15.988 --> 00:09:17.956
I heard about it this morning.

00:09:17.956 --> 00:09:21.260
-What do you mean you heard
about it this morning?

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:23.328
You're the president.
It's your budget.

00:09:23.328 --> 00:09:24.730
Who's running this place?

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:29.568
I don't want to be this guy,
but can you go get your manager?

00:09:29.568 --> 00:09:35.274
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:09:35.274 --> 00:09:39.978
And then, on Friday,
Trump just kept lying

00:09:39.978 --> 00:09:41.380
about the Special Olympics
fiasco.

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:44.082
During a Q&amp;A with reporters
at his resort in Palm Beach,

00:09:44.082 --> 00:09:45.618
Trump was asked
about his decision

00:09:45.618 --> 00:09:47.553
to overrule sanctions
on North Korea

00:09:47.553 --> 00:09:49.788
that his own administration
wanted to implement,

00:09:49.788 --> 00:09:52.057
and he compared the situation
to the Special Olympics

00:09:52.057 --> 00:09:53.959
by once again lying about it.

00:09:53.959 --> 00:09:57.696
-I just decided
that I would not let it happen.

00:09:57.696 --> 00:10:00.132
In a certain way,
it's like the Special Olympics.

00:10:00.132 --> 00:10:02.634
For many years,
it hasn't been approved,

00:10:02.634 --> 00:10:06.271
and then, at some point, it gets
negotiated out in Congress.

00:10:06.271 --> 00:10:09.808
Well, I went out, and I said,
"We're gonna have funding

00:10:09.808 --> 00:10:11.276
for the Special Olympics.

00:10:11.276 --> 00:10:12.578
-You didn't save it!

00:10:12.578 --> 00:10:14.680
You're the one
who proposed the cut!

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:17.082
Where is your manager?!

00:10:17.082 --> 00:10:18.517
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:10:18.517 --> 00:10:20.786
Trump lies like this...

00:10:20.786 --> 00:10:22.254
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:10:22.254 --> 00:10:23.722
He lies like this
about everything.

00:10:23.722 --> 00:10:25.791
In fact, this isn't even
the only budget item

00:10:25.791 --> 00:10:26.992
Trump has lied about this week.

00:10:26.992 --> 00:10:28.561
Just take something as innocuous

00:10:28.561 --> 00:10:30.663
as The Great Lakes
Restoration Initiative,

00:10:30.663 --> 00:10:33.398
which was first implemented
by Obama in 2010.

00:10:33.398 --> 00:10:35.968
Trump requested no funding
at all for this initiative

00:10:35.968 --> 00:10:37.937
in his 2018 budget request,

00:10:37.937 --> 00:10:39.638
effectively eliminating
the program.

00:10:39.638 --> 00:10:42.941
His latest budget proposes
a 90% cut to the program.

00:10:42.941 --> 00:10:45.177
And yet at a rally
in Michigan last week,

00:10:45.177 --> 00:10:47.245
Trump told his supporters
he was totally committed

00:10:47.245 --> 00:10:49.581
to funding the program
while also making clear

00:10:49.581 --> 00:10:52.218
he knows absolutely nothing
about the Great Lakes.

00:10:52.218 --> 00:10:54.353
-I support the Great Lakes.

00:10:54.353 --> 00:10:55.488
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:55.488 --> 00:10:58.257
Always have.

00:10:58.257 --> 00:11:02.394
They're beautiful.
They're big, very deep.

00:11:02.394 --> 00:11:04.429
Record deepness, right?

00:11:04.429 --> 00:11:08.433
-I am -- I'm sorry, but I have
a hard time believing

00:11:08.433 --> 00:11:10.870
you have always supported
the Great Lakes.

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:12.170
[ Laughter ]

00:11:12.170 --> 00:11:15.808
You grew up in Queens and worked
in Manhattan real estate.

00:11:15.808 --> 00:11:17.910
"As a little boy,
I loved two things --

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:21.080
giant gold buildings
and the lakes in the Midwest."

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:22.348
[ Laughter ]

00:11:22.348 --> 00:11:25.484
"I know them all --
Huron, Michelen, Eric,

00:11:25.484 --> 00:11:27.319
Titicaca, and Inferior."

00:11:27.319 --> 00:11:29.688
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:29.688 --> 00:11:31.189
You...

00:11:31.189 --> 00:11:33.925
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:11:33.925 --> 00:11:36.361
When it comes to lakes,
you're out of your depth,

00:11:36.361 --> 00:11:38.063
or should I say,
you're out of your...

00:11:38.063 --> 00:11:39.431
-Deepness.

00:11:39.431 --> 00:11:40.465
[ Laughter ]

00:11:40.465 --> 00:11:42.934
-Trump did the same thing

00:11:42.934 --> 00:11:45.837
while rambling about wind energy
at the same rally.

00:11:45.837 --> 00:11:47.540
He bragged
about energy production

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:49.274
under his administration,
and for some reason,

00:11:49.274 --> 00:11:51.110
he decided to go
on an extended rant

00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:53.145
about how much he knows
about wind.

00:11:53.145 --> 00:11:55.347
-If Hillary got in,
you wouldn't have that stat,

00:11:55.347 --> 00:11:57.082
I can tell you right now.

00:11:57.082 --> 00:12:00.653
You'd be doing wind, windmills.
Weeend!

00:12:00.653 --> 00:12:02.455
[ Laughter ]

00:12:02.455 --> 00:12:03.656
-If there's one thing
we've learned

00:12:03.656 --> 00:12:05.390
about Trump's presidency so far,

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:07.960
it's that he loves
doing random sound effects.

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:10.095
-Weeend!
Shoom!

00:12:10.095 --> 00:12:12.565
Whuh-huh-huh.
Bink.

00:12:12.565 --> 00:12:13.965
[ Laughter ]

00:12:13.965 --> 00:12:15.601
-That's the whole presidency
right there.

00:12:15.601 --> 00:12:17.969
He lies about funding
for the Special Olympics

00:12:17.969 --> 00:12:19.839
and tries to take away
his voters' healthcare,

00:12:19.839 --> 00:12:21.340
but they love his sound effects.

00:12:21.340 --> 00:12:24.075
We're living through
the "Police Academy" presidency.

00:12:24.075 --> 00:12:27.980
[ Warbling, imitated gunfire,
trilling ]

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:30.916
Mueller's report may not have
established Russian collusion,

00:12:30.916 --> 00:12:32.618
but it exposed
a whole world of corruption

00:12:32.618 --> 00:12:33.852
most people didn't know about.

00:12:33.852 --> 00:12:35.687
Donald Trump isn't working
for another country.

00:12:35.687 --> 00:12:37.055
He's working for himself.

00:12:37.055 --> 00:12:38.524
He's enriching himself
while trying

00:12:38.524 --> 00:12:39.825
to take healthcare
away from millions.

00:12:39.825 --> 00:12:41.893
In other words, we're in deep.

00:12:41.893 --> 00:12:43.095
-Record deepness.

00:12:43.095 --> 00:12:44.963
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:12:44.963 --> 00:12:48.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

